    <DataNode elementId="AT1G06820-MONOMER" textLabel="carotene isomerase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9M9Y8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Mutants affected in the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana CRTISO&lt;/i&gt; gene accumulate acyclic, poly-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-carotene precursors: |FRAME:CPD-7496 prolycopene|, |FRAME:CPD-7524 7,9,9&apos;-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-neurosporene| and a mix of &amp;zeta;-carotene isomers |CITS:[11884677]|. The accumulation of these compounds leads to a distinctive orange-yellow coloration of the cotyledons, in constrast with the yellow coloration of those of wild type. The accumulation of &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-carotenes rapidly disappears upon exposure to light. The protein responsible for this mutant phenotype was identified as a carotenoid isomerase. Its activity was confirmed by heterologous expression in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;: extracts of mutant, dark-grown &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; mutants were co-incubated with recombinant CRTISO-expressing &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; extracts; the mixture was shown to consistently contain an increase in |FRAME:CPD1F-114 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-lycopene|, |FRAME:NEUROSPORENE neurosporene| and |FRAME:CPD1F-98 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene| |CITS:[11884677]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G06820-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G06820.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9M9Y8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_172167" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-17898, RXN-17897, RXN-12784" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G06820.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G06820" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11884677" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G10830-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G10830-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="B3H769" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">The reaction catalyzed by this |FRAME: AT1G10830-MONOMER &amp;zeta;-carotene isomerase| is one of four redox reactions that are coupled to an electron transport chain and convert the colorless |FRAME: CPD-12321 15-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytoene| to the red-colored |FRAME: CPD1F-114 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-lycopene|. While this reaction can be catalyzed by light, it is also catalyzed enzymatically, as |FRAME: CPD1F-114 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-lycopene| biosynthesis can occur in the dark. The |FRAME: AT1G10830 Z-ISO| gene has been identified by analyzing mutants that accumulated |FRAME: CPD-7535 9,15,9&apos;-tri-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene| in the dark |CITS: [20335404]|. Sequence comparison for 12 candidate genes pointed to only one mutated gene, |FRAME: AT1G10830 &quot;At1g10830&quot;|. Transcript levels were induced by light and reduced by night extension. The highest transcript levels were detected in leaf. The protein is localized in the chloroplast. To demonstrate the function of the gene, an E. coli complementation platform was utilized. Using this system, it was demonstrated that |FRAME:CPD-7535 9,15,9&apos;-tri-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene| was converted to |FRAME:CPD-7526 9,9&apos;-di-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene| only in the presence of the gene |CITS: [20335404]|. Similar sequences were found in higher and lower plants, algae, diatoms, and cyanobacteria. The function of the maize homolog was directly demonstrated by an in vitro activity assay with purified recombinant protein |CITS: [26075523]|. The isomerase activity was controlled by redox state. The maize enzyme was functional only in its reduced form, and was shown to be a heme-containing enzyme.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G10830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G10830.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="B3H769" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-17694" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G10830.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G10830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="31.767" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightSeq" value="31.767" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20335404" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_26075523" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G57030-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G57030-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38932" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding the &amp;epsilon;-cyclase catalyzing the cyclization of lycopene was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and recombinant expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. It was demonstrated that the &amp;epsilon;-cyclase added one ring forming the monocyclic &amp;delta;-carotene but was unable to introduce a second &amp;epsilon; ring |CITS: [8837512]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G57030-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G57030.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAB53336" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q38932" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AT5G57030" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33993, RXN-1F-99" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G57030.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G57030" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Pi" value="5.7" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_8837512" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G15110.1" textLabel="AT4G15110.1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G15110.1" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
