    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G10230-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G10230-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38933" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Encodes a protein with lycopene &amp;beta;-cyclase activity. This enzyme uses the linear, symmetrical lycopene as substrate. The enzyme introduces a ring at both ends of lycopene to form the bicyclic |FRAME:CPD1F-129| (&lt;i&gt;via&lt;/i&gt; the formation of the intermediate |FRAME:CPD1F-126|). The |FRAME:AT3G10230| gene from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; was recombinantly expressed in engineered &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; strains modified to produced neurosporene or lycopene. In the former, the gene product led to the formation of |FRAME:CPD-7419|, whilst in the latter case, it led to the formation of &amp;beta;-carotene with no detectable &amp;gamma;-intermediate |CITS:[8837512]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G10230-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G10230.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_187634" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q38933" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33785, RXN-5308" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G10230.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G10230" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Pi" value="5.7" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_8837512" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G31800-MONOMER" textLabel="carotene beta-ring hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q56YV8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A number of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; mutants affected in the &lt;i&gt;LUT5&lt;/i&gt; gene were shown to be defective in the production of lutein (18% reduction) and accumulates two lutein biosynthesis-intermediate compounds: |FRAME:CPD1F-118| and |FRAME:CPD-7421|. Moreover, a reduction in total amounts of &amp;beta;,&amp;beta;-carotenoids is observed alongside an increase in total &amp;beta;,&amp;epsilon;-carotenoids |CITS:[16492736]|. It is therefore thought that the protein encoded by this gene possesses &amp;beta;-ring hydroxylase activity |CITS:[16492736]|. The enzyme has not been purified and characterized.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G31800-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G31800.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_564384" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q56YV8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Swissmodel" value="Q56YV8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Modbase" value="Q56YV8" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP97A3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="&amp;beta;-ring carotenoid hydroxylase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="&amp;beta;-hydroxylase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33614, RXN-33613, RXN-12570" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G31800.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G31800" />
