    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G52570-MONOMER" textLabel="Beta-carotene 3-hydroxylase 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LTG0" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A second &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; &amp;beta;-hydroxylase shares 70% identity with the |FRAME:CPLX1F-106| previously identified |CITS:[11587509]|. The gene was isolated and expressed in recombinant &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; strains engineered to accumulate &amp;beta;- or &amp;epsilon;-carotenes: in a &amp;beta;-carotene-accumulating background, the &amp;beta;-hydroxylase 2 cDNA produced 90% |FRAME:CPD1F-130| and 6% of |FRAME:CPD-7409| intermediate; in an &amp;epsilon;-carotene-accumulating background (&amp;delta;-carotene), the cDNA produced only small amounts (&lt;6%) of the hydroxylated product: |FRAME:CPD-7413| |CITS:[11587509]|. The enzyme was not tested for its ability to hydroxylase |FRAME:CPD1F-118|, but it is hypothesized that it can perform this activity |CITS:[12782726]|. Moreover, mutants deficient in the production of this enzyme were isolated and shown to be defective in the production of &amp;beta;-ring hydroxylated carotenoids. The mere depletion of one gene does not suffice to abolish the activity as a degree of genetic redundancy was observed for this activity |CITS:[12782726]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G52570-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G52570.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_200070" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9LTG0" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtB2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12672, RXN-12741, RXN-12742, RXN-6445" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
