      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">This enzyme is involved in carotenoid biosynthesis in plants and cyanobacteria. The enzyme from Synechococcus can also use NAD+ and NADP+ as electron acceptor under anaerobic conditions. The enzyme from Gentiana lutea shows no activity with NAD+ or NADP+ |CITS: [11714315]|. This is one of two reactions catalyzed successively by the enzyme. The overall reaction is |FRAME: RXN-11355 15-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-phytoene + 2 a plastoquinone = 9,15,9&apos;-tri-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;zeta;-carotene + 2 a plastoquinol|</Comment>
