  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX1F-19" textLabel="CPLX1F-19" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX1F-19" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="335" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>In light &amp;zeta;-Carotene meets the stereospecific requirements of &amp;zeta;-carotene desaturase and pro-lycopene is formed. The enzyme has been recombinantly expressed and purified in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and its function demonstrated |CITS: [9914519]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX1F-19" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G04870-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33777, RXN-12728, RXN-17699, RXN-17882, RXN-12729, RXN-ARA-12728" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="6" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_9914519" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX1F-29" textLabel="CPLX1F-29" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="Q8RXE6" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The epoxidation reaction of the xanthophyll cycle consists of the conversion of zeaxanthin to antheraxanthin and violaxanthin and is carried out by the zeaxanthin epoxidase. The isolated cDNA for this enzyme from tobacco was used to identify potential epoxidases of other plants. The cDNA of Arabidopsis thaliana (GenBank CAB41869) shows strong sequence homology to lipocalin proteins including the zeaxanthin epoxidase |CITS: [11058750]|. It has been demonstrated that in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; plants defective in osmotic stress-regulated gene induction the LOS6/ABA1 gene encodes a zeaxanthin epoxidase that functions in ABA biosynthesis |CITS: [11779861]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX1F-29" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_201504" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8RXE6" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="antheraxanthin epoxidase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G67030-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33580, RXN-12755, RXN-12754" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009534" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCO-CHLOR-THY" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11779861" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11058750" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX1F-106" textLabel="CPLX1F-106" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SZZ8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="495" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>A cDNA encoding the &amp;beta;-carotene hydroxylase was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and its function verified by functional complementation in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme specifically acted on the &amp;beta;-ring of the carotenoids forming &amp;beta;-cryptoxanthin and subsequently zeaxanthin from &amp;beta;-carotene |CITS: [8798688]|. The enzyme was also shown to catalyze the hydroxylation of the monocyclic |FRAME:CPD-7419| |CITS:[8798688]|. In an &amp;epsilon;-carotene-accumulating background (&amp;delta;-carotene), the cDNA produced only small amounts of the hydroxylated product: |FRAME:CPD-7413| |CITS:[8798688]|. The enzyme was not tested for its ability to hydroxylase |FRAME:CPD1F-118|, but it is hypothesized that it can perform this activity |CITS:[12782726]|. It has been suggested that the protein might form a homodimer |CITS:[8798688]|. Moreover, mutants deficient in the production of this enzyme were isolated and shown to be defective in the production of &amp;beta;-ring hydroxylated carotenoids. The mere depletion of one gene does not suffice to abolish the activity as a degree of genetic redundancy was observed for this activity |CITS:[12782726]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX1F-106" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAC49443" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SZZ8" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CHYb1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="&amp;beta;-hydroxylase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="&amp;beta;-ring carotenoid hydroxylase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT4G25700-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33870, RXN-12736, RXN-12737" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009536" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCO-PLASTID" />
      <Property key="Pi" value="9.4" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12782726" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_8798688" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
